  "generated_text": "To find the area of the pentagon, we can break it down into simpler shapes whose areas we can calculate easily, such as triangles and rectangles. The pentagon can be divided into a rectangle and a right triangle.\n\nFirst, let's identify the dimensions of the rectangle and the right triangle. The rectangle has a width of 8 inches and a height of 12 inches. The right triangle has a base of 8 inches and a height of 6 inches.\n\nThe area of the rectangle is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of the rectangle} = \\text{width} \\times \\text{height} = 8 \\times 12 = 96 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the area of the right triangle. The area of a right triangle is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of the triangle} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times 6 = 24 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nThe total area of the pentagon is the sum of the areas of the rectangle and the triangle:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of the pentagon} = \\text{Area of the rectangle} + \\text{Area of the triangle} = 96 + 24 = 120 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the pentagon is \\(\\boxed{120}\\).",
